# C: bonds. The Foundation controls Mozilla.org; Mozilla.org owns the four operating companies and backs Mozilla Data Collective. Each is mirrored in the other atom.
nodes:
  - id: C:bond/foundation-controls-org
    type: bond
    name: Foundation controls Mozilla.org
    summary: 'Mozilla.org stays within the umbrella of the Foundation: the Foundation appoints the majority of its board and consolidates it for financial reporting. The 2024 Form 990 Schedule R lists Mozilla.org (EIN 33-3437202) as a related tax-exempt organization whose direct controlling entity is the Foundation. Not an ownership bond: a non-profit has no shares.'
    kinds: [controls]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mozilla-org
    control: full
    basis: appoints the majority of the Mozilla.org board; consolidates it for financial reporting (Mozilla wiki, June 2026); Schedule R Part II, 2024
    accounting: consolidated
    inherits: [principles]
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/news/announcing-mozilla-org-new-non-profit/', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf'], confidence: 0.8, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/org-owns-corporation
    type: bond
    name: Mozilla.org owns the Corporation
    summary: Mozilla.org owns the Mozilla operating subsidiaries according to its FAQ; the Corporation, which makes Firefox, was a wholly owned taxable subsidiary of the Foundation until then.
    kinds: [owns]
    from: atom/mozilla-org
    to: atom/mozilla-corporation
    economic: 1.0
    voting: 1.0
    control: full
    basis: Mozilla.org owns the Mozilla operating subsidiaries (Mozilla wiki, June 2026); the Foundation held them at 100% in the audited 2024 statements and the 2024 Form 990 Schedule R
    accounting: consolidated
    nci: 0
    inherits: [principles]
    pending: The audited 2024 statements and the 2024 Form 990 give 100% held by the Foundation; the June 2026 Mozilla.org FAQ says Mozilla.org owns the operating subsidiaries without restating the share or the date of transfer. 100% is carried over from the last filing.
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf', 'https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/governance/organizations/'], confidence: 0.6, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/org-owns-mzla
    type: bond
    name: Mozilla.org owns MZLA
    summary: Thunderbird's donate page says MZLA is a wholly owned for-profit subsidiary of the not-for-profit Mozilla.org, and its about page says Thunderbird operates in a separate for-profit subsidiary of Mozilla.org; the 2024 filings and the May 2025 privacy notice had MZLA wholly owned by the Foundation.
    kinds: [owns]
    from: atom/mozilla-org
    to: atom/mzla
    economic: 1.0
    voting: 1.0
    control: full
    basis: 'Thunderbird donate page: a wholly owned for-profit subsidiary of the not-for-profit Mozilla.org; the Foundation held it at 100% in the 2024 filings'
    accounting: consolidated
    nci: 0
    inherits: [principles]
    since: {pending: 'date the shares moved to Mozilla.org: the FAQ says 2026, not when'}
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/donate/', 'https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/about/', 'https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/org-owns-mozilla-ai
    type: bond
    name: Mozilla.org owns Mozilla.ai
    summary: MZL.AI, PBC was wholly owned by the Foundation in the 2024 filings; the Mozilla.ai pages still say it is backed by the Foundation.
    kinds: [owns]
    from: atom/mozilla-org
    to: atom/mozilla-ai
    economic: 1.0
    voting: 1.0
    control: full
    basis: Mozilla.org owns the Mozilla operating subsidiaries (Mozilla wiki, June 2026); the Foundation held them at 100% in the audited 2024 statements and the 2024 Form 990 Schedule R
    accounting: consolidated
    nci: 0
    inherits: [principles]
    pending: The audited 2024 statements and the 2024 Form 990 give 100% held by the Foundation; the June 2026 Mozilla.org FAQ says Mozilla.org owns the operating subsidiaries without restating the share or the date of transfer. 100% is carried over from the last filing.
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf', 'https://mozilla.ai/company/about-us'], confidence: 0.6, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/org-owns-ventures
    type: bond
    name: Mozilla.org owns Mozilla Ventures Management
    summary: Mozilla Ventures Management, PBC, the fund's manager, was wholly owned by the Foundation in the 2024 filings; the fund itself is a limited partnership whose sole partner, in the first fund, is Mozilla.
    kinds: [owns]
    from: atom/mozilla-org
    to: atom/mozilla-ventures
    economic: 1.0
    voting: 1.0
    control: full
    basis: Mozilla.org owns the Mozilla operating subsidiaries (Mozilla wiki, June 2026); the Foundation held them at 100% in the audited 2024 statements and the 2024 Form 990 Schedule R
    accounting: consolidated
    nci: 0
    inherits: [principles]
    pending: The audited 2024 statements and the 2024 Form 990 give 100% held by the Foundation; the June 2026 Mozilla.org FAQ says Mozilla.org owns the operating subsidiaries without restating the share or the date of transfer. 100% is carried over from the last filing.
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf'], confidence: 0.6, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/org-backs-mdc
    type: bond
    name: Mozilla.org backs Mozilla Data Collective
    summary: Mozilla Data Collective calls itself backed by the not-for-profit Mozilla.org. Companies House lists no registrable person or entity with significant control (statement of 2026-02-25), so no ownership share is recorded.
    kinds: [affiliated]
    from: atom/mozilla-org
    to: atom/mozilla-data-collective
    control: none
    pending: How is Mozilla Data Collective Limited owned? "Mission-locked" is not defined on its pages and Companies House shows no controller.
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://mozilladatacollective.com/', 'https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/17054959', 'https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/17054959/persons-with-significant-control', 'https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org'], confidence: 0.7, state: known}
